{
 "_about": "W1-BIOME per-climate ground look, one entry per climates.json key. textures: baked by tools/blender/terrain/bake_terrain.py (final albedo). palette: shader multipliers on those textures (white = as baked; dry/wet/mud/bare/ash are multipliers on ground/sand/dirt/rock; shallow and deep are absolute colours). ground_cover: low vegetation families the scatter may place. palm_allowlist: palm families allowed. special_tiles: tile overrides the terrain may stamp. Hooked into islands by W2-TERRAIN/W2-SCATTER. special_families: island_runtime _spawn_special_family families the scatter may place; berry_bush only where the climate's vegetation has BushBerries (world-placement-08: berries on volcano). compat_gain: multiplier on the ground tints under gl_compatibility only, where bright sets clip.",
 "water_only_families": [
  "Lilypad"
 ],
 "zones_about": "Biome zones, painted per tile into the tile map's G channel (BiomeZones). id = palette column. tint multiplies the climate's baked ground texture, mix weights the four layers (ground/dirt/sand/rock), map is the minimap/atlas colour, node_mult/prop_mult scale resource and prop family densities. A climate's zones.{base,lush,dry} name which zone a low-moisture, wet and dry patch becomes; weights are relative shares of land and are normalised at load.",
